    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and mirroring the existing `customerCode` machinery.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter, next to `customerCode`.\n2. **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor function that reads the owner via `@Val`, computes `customerCode + \"-M\" + <2-digit year>`, and sets it. `String.format(\"%02d\", year % 100)` guarantees the two-digit, zero-padded `YY`.\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `assignCustomerCode` (so both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are already set), under the same `transaction` governance, feeding into `assignNamesakeCount`.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it into the JSON the test reads (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column (tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema script).\n\nTest result: `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest` (`coreMembershipNumberFormat`) passing (1 run, 0 failures).",
